      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The loss of traditional craftsmanship and aesthetic appeal can indeed dilute the value of an artwork, reducing it to a mere soundbite or message rather than a comprehensive and nuanced experience. In the end, art should strive to stand on its own merit, regardless of its message, as you've pointed out that \"acts of propaganda\" would be more effective through other mediums, like journalism. A successful artwork should transcend its pedagogical purpose to speak directly to the viewer's emotions and intellect.",
